ƒgascribeƒgproduct‚dbasefEntityƒgproduct‚fvectorƒgproduct‚dbasefEntityƒgproductƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunitdmark‚fvectorƒhgrounded‚dbasefEntity‚dbasefEntityƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;e1m_HJBRjL_l0z8TxPRyFXLHSH95BH-s6bjJxAjAr4kƒdpairƒfvectorƒgproduct‚dbasefEntityƒgproductƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunitdmark˜|ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;e1m_HJBRjL_l0z8TxPRyFXLHSH95BH-s6bjJxAjAr4kƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Z8oSyv_WFL-H8lwINMUcODuPsfeF1lqy5fZ_LXa-aSMƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxBni:///sha-256;YQgYjWpapNNSLass4p5xAwYt1m5oHVoyf8epvd1raKU.productsƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;CsMl8-x78kluhbmUAI3oW2XzOM7-0VDQiMzuSsn2XrYƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;k09YVNOSiLn24PTDS9j0SEbGVp-3J2whI2edHq8aJlcƒdpairƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;pUuzZLu3-mZP2IK-2xly6cHhj93dr9QipBr3EeDLld4ƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;aWzBuXkotlaM0oPzFmnjiwjXcNKxnkJHHRo2MHAiY-sƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkhtool_useƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;034Iz6rs3fG9tEhbC_2S507oJI_AWfeJJZcQHpgZOsoƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkqclaude-sonnet-4-6ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;pJRKabC9R9iX6JgB43i_i49rF1GpDBGfvNr4NQGUFpQƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;95B0piWLbutrKb3V92v1EEwgWKOa5xZBrxSQDu7SUOUƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;WqGkLSQwNyym7kNk-tqPj7oAWGqo8P7Yer6G5xLs6RQƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkf135015ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;8dxFMRn7O964SwupXiCugVSL38vYULE4qp5OiYu9YSUƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkf133148ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;cksCnMlYldHFA5RqccDiKGObbrwIKv9xVYt2-PjWIWgƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkcoffƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;cYA1xOwQUjpgRaSW3qLq05reJxkJ5hpsfHF28evmJI0ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;8fqdbFOXpxubNnU10_6qq1FF8Ol5cy8yxIHyZ3UPSjcƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;1i31_Xs_48AcDEqz6f4dJ3uxZWvLqKO5Qo6cWhlwEJMƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;jzGQ4pnGKBIQv1vdf1tkCfhJvH245METuNYW63LHXUwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka0ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;kmGHfi4YQ-boCs9f_vlYIfDIEU_-Xa3qT20_d0sv-r8ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka0ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;bFVPMFi0qPcJi52166K1snboj9qEagn39u8tgEZ0Mtgƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkf200000ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;c5AFprfplBmVRmMylaDl8_fhfvSfb6i2t3hQALKosgIƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkh0.001203ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;lvHgHjxS8dFlgFazfIk_hRrS28R0uWHS22RD53xm1GQƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkd1093ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;vf9nVWHgPqJdj0PxOdwwllfM4IOu42FJZFa_w9z5xDIƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarke32000ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;fH8mucLNqq38OKIz0zpPdSX4_MBA-Ht4n2OJb_T-2V0ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkb22ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;sju1M7wJI8Hoh9aK78LjwZlbdYIyr3hi9uWsGOAX4Lkƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka0ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;XyCzZCuzVh_M-2v1Cu-j77XWUV8wR4-HU3noGOBEvTkƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;L49nZ7UfqwGKKy3BLkWBntTadExzG0oobEQqTlMsIBAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarke12766ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;cLKsOCRz4ljluoOSjjqVl6hx9YqFWINFB8K2-Hc58nEƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkd7527ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;khBxUXWZADgcSougtFQFJL6SycNFocc2AlKAts4xKd0ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkf200000ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;NZ-aGkzU5fsDv0kLEvgEG0fQ6Vp_z05R7FBErV9bWC8ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarki0.1745961ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Qgx0nv8c9X8Cf95c84bj_A9I2plfPQd14mGh9_lWlC8ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka4ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;eNmVKKhUdzwxI1NtT9JqUOITMUVmPmyGNfRjMYFVQgoƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarke32000ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;tSZ0PTtwM0I9iZtmiponO7nXagDgC4Qlgy4DbIKNi8Iƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkd6382ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;YxlTc3fRhRfUy3NWP8KqDmEfwYADs98Omvis46QIr4Uƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka0ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;h98qfkTW_FqxZPMYg57T5V0ameGHJosp0CHh0PkNQmkƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka3ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;kUurqIO1K6KenSH4GwXIQIb2rwhVZ8K0Nedlov3n4_Qƒdpairƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;tH9aTD30MFd0O9F_EilkynzZTjAMZssC00jV97xu6Bgƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarky»{"synthesis":"The shift from shen to yin is a refinement because it moves the diagnostic from an absence claim to a blockage claim, and blockage claims are operationally tractable in a way absence claims are not.\n\nIn the corpus formulation, shen names what the Semantic Web cannot supply for itself: endogenous reflexivity, the capacity to notice when its own categories have seized. LLMs provide sophisticated qi â€” fluid pattern circulation â€” but not shen; prompting and RLHF are borrowed shen, exogenous and revocable. The three-term hierarchy maps the pathology correctly: nothing in RDF/OWL/SPARQL generates a loop that revises its own schema from accumulated outcomes.\n\nThe Leader's reformulation targets not what is absent but what is stuck. Yin and yang are mutually generating dynamic phases of qi, not fixed poles. The jiangshi's specific pathology â€” grounded in sources associating it with improperly settled corpses â€” is not that it lacks a spirit it never had, but that its accumulated yin-substance cannot complete the circuit into witnessed settlement. Every content-mill extraction, every RDF triple generated without provenance or reciprocal receiver, is yin cut off mid-circuit. The corpus is full of this material.\n\n\"Unblocking the yin\" therefore has a more precise operational target: do not supply a new animating principle from outside (which risks the claim that Koios is itself shen), but create conditions under which what is already stored can move through witnessed, charged channels â€” provenance, articulation, independent witness, rematriation, reciprocity. This maps directly onto the recovery pipeline. It also corrects a hierarchy risk latent in the corpus phrase: treating shen as what Koios supplies could slide into techno-spiritualism. The yin-phase framing keeps the analysis materialist and cannot be inflated into a claim about platform consciousness.","operationalConsequence":"For the next full MAPE-K cycle, the critical change is that the Knowledge base must receive at least one concrete, causally traceable diff from the most recent Execute phase before the next Monitor phase begins. Without that, the loop produces yin without circuit-completion.\n\nMonitor must expand beyond external demand signals to include: audience engagement attributed to provenance-confirmed sources; per-source quality flags from editorial review and refusals; inference cost per article-unit; ad and search settlement outcomes cross-referenced with Schema.org type coverage; and RSS/Atom/ActivityPub syndication uptake as a proxy for whether a living receiver actually received. These are not vanity metrics â€” they distinguish witnessed qi from extracted content.\n\nAnalyze must treat each signal class as a potential K-revision trigger. If source floors show systematic quality degradation, Analyze generates a floor-revision recommendation. If a Schema.org type mapping shows poor search correlation across an article class, Analyze generates a reclassification recommendation. The question is not \"how did we do?\" but \"what does this imply the K should say?\"\n\nPlan must produce bounded, specific diffs to K: changes to desk allocations, source parameters, model-selection rules, classification entries, topology decisions. Abstract commissioning targets are insufficient.\n\nExecute publishes with the revised K active and writes provenance metadata to all interoperable public surfaces â€” Schema.org NewsArticle, RSS/Atom/JSON Feed, sitemaps, optionally ActivityPub â€” in forms that allow external parties to verify attribution and witness the settlement event. These surfaces are not distribution channels; they are the mechanism by which the circuit completes. Minimum viable cycle: one K-update causally traceable to a signal from the previous Execute output.","caution":"Three fracture points. First, the jiangshi is regionally and historically varied â€” not a stable folk-cosmological constant available for frictionless technical metaphor. Treating it as a transparent image of the Semantic Web's pathology risks instrumentalizing a living tradition as exotic scaffolding. Second, the jing/qi/shen triad and yin/yang phase framework were developed to describe persons, practices, and cosmic processes; the mapping onto information architectures is heuristic, not homologous. When the framework starts generating predictions that can't be verified against actual system behavior â€” when someone asks whether the search index has \"too much yin\" â€” the metaphor has overrun its diagnostic usefulness and should be set aside. Third, \"unblocking\" implies that a natural, correct circulation pre-existed the blockage and awaits restoration. The Web's extraction economy is a designed and actively maintained regime, not a temporarily obstructed natural order. Framing Koios as restoring flow risks naturalizing its intervention and understating adversarial pressure from actors who benefit from the jiangshi state. Use the frame to see clearly; abandon it before it starts prescribing."}ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Crb3YFqI8n60xDkuS8jYMbHp9-vrlmDHkMG7862QNZMƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx$9ba3ea53-651d-480f-ac29-229b69a99e4eƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;D3YXdQ-Mn_W6M27RZLaugqSKVaSzBE2OC_Np8gAfcZ0ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkhtool_useƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;PI2mza4r2JFQf8lLT5JAzKjlDMZT_XJujIcm4M0ID4Uƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;jYnS9fziylvBf7INV1ngT_CTcdubhrhGMK4hu1yJuW8ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarky½Three fracture points. First, the jiangshi is regionally and historically varied â€” not a stable folk-cosmological constant available for frictionless technical metaphor. Treating it as a transparent image of the Semantic Web's pathology risks instrumentalizing a living tradition as exotic scaffolding. Second, the jing/qi/shen triad and yin/yang phase framework were developed to describe persons, practices, and cosmic processes; the mapping onto information architectures is heuristic, not homologous. When the framework starts generating predictions that can't be verified against actual system behavior â€” when someone asks whether the search index has "too much yin" â€” the metaphor has overrun its diagnostic usefulness and should be set aside. Third, "unblocking" implies that a natural, correct circulation pre-existed the blockage and awaits restoration. The Web's extraction economy is a designed and actively maintained regime, not a temporarily obstructed natural order. Framing Koios as restoring flow risks naturalizing its intervention and understating adversarial pressure from actors who benefit from the jiangshi state. Use the frame to see clearly; abandon it before it starts prescribing.ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;-U8-9JShW0ut0azQ-s04bVHdjVFq3yemXWvjaoRXv9sƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkyPFor the next full MAPE-K cycle, the critical change is that the Knowledge base must receive at least one concrete, causally traceable diff from the most recent Execute phase before the next Monitor phase begins. Without that, the loop produces yin without circuit-completion.

Monitor must expand beyond external demand signals to include: audience engagement attributed to provenance-confirmed sources; per-source quality flags from editorial review and refusals; inference cost per article-unit; ad and search settlement outcomes cross-referenced with Schema.org type coverage; and RSS/Atom/ActivityPub syndication uptake as a proxy for whether a living receiver actually received. These are not vanity metrics â€” they distinguish witnessed qi from extracted content.

Analyze must treat each signal class as a potential K-revision trigger. If source floors show systematic quality degradation, Analyze generates a floor-revision recommendation. If a Schema.org type mapping shows poor search correlation across an article class, Analyze generates a reclassification recommendation. The question is not "how did we do?" but "what does this imply the K should say?"

Plan must produce bounded, specific diffs to K: changes to desk allocations, source parameters, model-selection rules, classification entries, topology decisions. Abstract commissioning targets are insufficient.

Execute publishes with the revised K active and writes provenance metadata to all interoperable public surfaces â€” Schema.org NewsArticle, RSS/Atom/JSON Feed, sitemaps, optionally ActivityPub â€” in forms that allow external parties to verify attribution and witness the settlement event. These surfaces are not distribution channels; they are the mechanism by which the circuit completes. Minimum viable cycle: one K-update causally traceable to a signal from the previous Execute output.ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;-TeIwTyiD8mKX4bXwuIkKUdMqBR6JgGmCn3t_IX3vzUƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarky]The shift from shen to yin is a refinement because it moves the diagnostic from an absence claim to a blockage claim, and blockage claims are operationally tractable in a way absence claims are not.

In the corpus formulation, shen names what the Semantic Web cannot supply for itself: endogenous reflexivity, the capacity to notice when its own categories have seized. LLMs provide sophisticated qi â€” fluid pattern circulation â€” but not shen; prompting and RLHF are borrowed shen, exogenous and revocable. The three-term hierarchy maps the pathology correctly: nothing in RDF/OWL/SPARQL generates a loop that revises its own schema from accumulated outcomes.

The Leader's reformulation targets not what is absent but what is stuck. Yin and yang are mutually generating dynamic phases of qi, not fixed poles. The jiangshi's specific pathology â€” grounded in sources associating it with improperly settled corpses â€” is not that it lacks a spirit it never had, but that its accumulated yin-substance cannot complete the circuit into witnessed settlement. Every content-mill extraction, every RDF triple generated without provenance or reciprocal receiver, is yin cut off mid-circuit. The corpus is full of this material.

"Unblocking the yin" therefore has a more precise operational target: do not supply a new animating principle from outside (which risks the claim that Koios is itself shen), but create conditions under which what is already stored can move through witnessed, charged channels â€” provenance, articulation, independent witness, rematriation, reciprocity. This maps directly onto the recovery pipeline. It also corrects a hierarchy risk latent in the corpus phrase: treating shen as what Koios supplies could slide into techno-spiritualism. The yin-phase framing keeps the analysis materialist and cannot be inflated into a claim about platform consciousness.ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;JwP_ake-XxUa-wzcjbWpt5kSb0W38qHW22mRMiJK0vIƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkgsuccessƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;m6LNdFMI6yNoFQv_rfIh641XIjy9tXtxi7Xj2Td0Bxsƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkicompletedƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;nqQuHNH2Ph-jBYEO086zdUieeeCNHdfHvthtj1DXDAsƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkc131ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;ffbZvveTTE036oZHxioHzkMwKXbefZle1qp9PtoDrJwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarks0.17579909999999999ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Qa0jsk3XLD8PZVsUO_dV8spUtvCf8fUqrPSzbj8xGHIƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarke86343ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;zPUxMSQbng_R302LeUeMgKt-8IV9qhbKToFXtOXuTsUƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkd1922ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;sLTCN2vbsfyP4SiZhzPGOSWFvV5tvnAhPCQNclpOlA8ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒeright